<%# Card left panel — shared by editor (surveys/show), preview
    (surveys/_preview_card), and player (player/_play_card).

    Locals:
      card     — the card hash
      progress — integer 0–100
      mode     — :editor, :preview, or :player (default: :preview)
%>
<%
  mode      ||= :preview
  editable   = (mode == :editor)
  has_lottie = card["lottie"].present?
  has_video  = card["video"].present?
  has_img    = card["image"].present?
  has_media  = has_video || has_img
  credit_word = has_video ? "Video by" : "Photo by"
  animate_asset = card["animate_asset"] == true
  is_range   = card["type"].to_s == "range"
  # An NPS card's animation is the liquid container on the ANSWER side, not
  # anything on this panel — but the CTA that changes it belongs here anyway,
  # with every other "change this card's asset" control, so a creator has one
  # place to look. Which means it has to survive all four media branches below
  # rather than living in one of them.
  is_nps     = card["type"].to_s == "nps"
%>

<%# The HEADER backdrop (card["media_bg"]) paints wherever the panel is not
    already covered by an opaque medium: behind an animation, and — since a
    creator asked to be able to design the phone view of an ordinary card — on a
    card carrying no media at all, where the panel IS the design. A photo or a
    video covers .split-left itself, so there is nothing to see behind one and
    nothing is offered. Falls through to the Verto-wide --brand-panel when the
    card hasn't set one.

    The class matters as much as the style: on a phone a card with no media has
    no hero strip at all (.split-left is display: contents, see the mobile block
    in application.css), so a backdrop with nothing to paint on would be a
    control that silently did nothing on the one surface it was asked for.
    .has-media-bg is what earns that card its strip back.

    This panel never carries the MOBILE BACKGROUND (card["mobile_bg"]) — that is
    .split-right's, in shared/_card_component: the area behind the question and
    answers, which starts where this header ends. Two fields, two elements. %>
<% has_media_bg = card_media_bg(card).present? %>
<div class="split-left<%= " has-asset-breathe" if animate_asset %><%= " has-media-bg" if has_media_bg %>" style="<%= card_media_bg_style(card) %>">
  <% if card["type"].to_s == "range" %>
    <%# Range: the LEFT panel plays a Lottie animation that swaps to match the
        slider position. The lottie-player controller listens for the
        `verto:scaleValue` event dispatched by the range slider on the right
        (its step index and count) and maps it onto its own set's frames — the
        age card's set has one per band, so every answer plays its own file.
        No initial_value — the helper defaults to the set's neutral middle
        frame, so the character starts expressionless (see
        NpsHelper::NPS_NEUTRAL_FRAME). %>
    <%= render_nps_reaction(theme: range_theme_slug(card)) %>
  <% elsif has_lottie %>
    <%# A pasted LottieFiles animation, stored same-origin by CardLottieStore
        and played on a loop. Its own class (card-lottie, not nps-lottie): the
        :has(.nps-lottie) CSS hides the Change-media CTA, which this keeps. %>
    <div class="card-lottie"<%= " data-card-media".html_safe if editable %>
         data-controller="lottie-player"
         data-lottie-player-urls-value="<%= [ card["lottie"] ].to_json %>"
         data-lottie-player-current-value="1"
         data-lottie-player-loop-value="true">
      <div class="card-lottie-mount" data-lottie-player-target="mount"></div>
    </div>
  <% elsif has_media %>
    <% if has_video %>
      <%# Autoplaying, looped, muted card video. preload="none" + poster keeps
          off-screen cards at zero bytes; the autoplay-video controller plays
          only while the card is on screen and pauses otherwise.

          A landscape clip in a portrait panel is cropped exactly like a photo,
          so it reads the same focal pair — via object-position, since the video
          is a real element rather than a painted background. Cropping it is not
          on the table (there is no canvas re-encode for a video), which is why
          "no crop on the videos" costs nothing: repositioning is the whole of
          what a video needs. %>
      <video class="split-left-video"<%= " data-card-media".html_safe if editable %>
             muted loop playsinline autoplay preload="none"
             data-controller="autoplay-video"
             style="<%= card_focal_style(card) %>"
             <% if card["video_poster"].present? %>poster="<%= card["video_poster"] %>"<% end %>>
        <source src="<%= card["video"] %>" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
    <% else %>
      <%# Each axis bites only where the frame crops that way: --focal-y in the
          mobile header strip and the device frames, --focal-x in the ordinary
          desktop panel. Both are always emitted so the editor's live drag has
          a property to rewrite. %>
      <div class="split-left-img"<%= " data-card-media".html_safe if editable %>
           data-controller="bg-image-healer"
           style="background-image:url('<%= card["image"] %>'); <%= card_focal_style(card) %>"></div>
    <% end %>
    <div class="split-left-overlay"<%= " data-card-media".html_safe if editable %>></div>
    <%# Subtle creator credit (Pexels picks). Doubles as the link back to
        Pexels the API guidelines ask for. %>
    <% if card["image_credit"].present? %>
      <div class="split-left-credit"<%= " data-card-media".html_safe if editable %>>
        <% if card["image_credit_url"].present? %>
          <a href="<%= card["image_credit_url"] %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow"><%= credit_word %> <%= card["image_credit"] %></a>
        <% else %>
          <%= credit_word %> <%= card["image_credit"] %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <div class="panel-progress">
    <div class="panel-progress-fill" style="width:<%= progress %>%;"></div>
  </div>

  <%# Editor: prompt the creator to add design (an image). The button stays in
      the DOM for every editor-mode card — including NPS — so type-switching
      in the editor (e.g. range → NPS → range) finds it ready to reappear.
      CSS hides it while a Lottie is mounted (.split-left:has(.nps-lottie) …).

      Every branch below ends its row with the SAME control, the Mobile
      background pill (shared/_mobile_background_cta): the area behind the
      question and answers on a phone is a design every card has, whatever
      this panel holds. The pills before it are this panel's — the header's —
      and each says so in its label, because the two used to share the one
      word "Background" and a creator could not tell which of the two screens'
      designs they were about to change. %>
  <% if editable %>
    <% if is_range %>
      <%# Range cards play a Lottie instead of an image — give the animation its
          own "change" CTA (the animation counterpart of the media picker), on
          the panel like every other asset's. A distinct class so the
          .split-left:has(.nps-lottie) rule that hides the image chrome leaves
          this one visible. A second CTA opens the ordinary media picker for
          the colour or image BEHIND the animation — the header's backdrop
          (media-picker#open already shows that section for a range card —
          _cardTakesBackground just checks the card type).
          The age card gets no such CTA: it plays its own bound set, one frame
          per band (NpsHelper::AGE_BAND_THEME), and a pick here would preview
          one animation and reload to another. %>
      <div class="split-left-cta-row">
        <%= render "shared/change_animation_cta", action: "open" unless NpsHelper.age_band_card?(card) %>
        <button type="button" class="add-bg-fab header-bg-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#open"
                title="<%= t("editor.header_background_title", default: "Colour or image behind this card's animation — the header on a phone") %>">
          <span><%= t("editor.header_background", default: "Header background") %></span>
        </button>
        <%= render "shared/mobile_background_cta" %>
      </div>
    <% elsif has_lottie %>
      <%# A Lottie is the one medium that can be TRANSPARENT, so what sits
          behind it is a real design decision rather than nothing — and this
          panel offered no way to make it ("I need the Change Background
          option here for when we upload transparent lottie files"). Only the
          entry point was missing: media-picker#_cardTakesBackground already
          returns true for any card carrying a lottie, not just for range, so
          the background section has been in that modal all along with nothing
          on this panel calling it.
          The one branch that gets no header-backdrop CTA is the next one down:
          a photo or a video is opaque, so a backdrop behind one is a control
          that does nothing. See ApplicationHelper#card_takes_backdrop?. %>
      <div class="split-left-cta-row">
        <%= render "shared/change_animation_cta", action: "openShapes" if is_nps %>
        <button type="button" class="add-media-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#open"
                title="<%= t("editor.change_media_title") %>">
          <span class="add-media-fab-plus">＋</span>
          <span><%= t("editor.change_media") %></span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="add-bg-fab header-bg-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#openCardBackground"
                title="<%= t("editor.header_background_title", default: "Colour or image behind this card's animation — the header on a phone") %>">
          <span><%= t("editor.header_background", default: "Header background") %></span>
        </button>
        <%= render "shared/mobile_background_cta" %>
      </div>
    <% elsif has_media %>
      <%# A card with media gets a second control: reframe what is already
          there instead of remove-and-reupload — Feedback 17, widened to "every
          image and piece of content", which is why it is no longer gated on
          the picture having been an upload. Drag to reposition works on any
          photo and on a video; the crop-and-zoom hand-off inside the stage is
          the part that needs a same-origin still. %>
      <div class="split-left-cta-row">
        <%= render "shared/change_animation_cta", action: "openShapes" if is_nps %>
        <button type="button" class="add-media-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#open"
                title="<%= t("editor.change_media_title") %>">
          <span class="add-media-fab-plus">＋</span>
          <span><%= t("editor.change_media") %></span>
        </button>
        <%# Always shown in this branch: reaching it means the panel carries a
            photo or a video, and repositioning is a stored background/object
            position rather than a re-encode — so unlike the crop it opens onto,
            it works on a Pexels URL and on a clip just as well as an upload.
            media_picker#_syncAdjustFab applies the same rule client-side when
            the media changes without a server render. %>
        <button type="button" class="add-bg-fab media-adjust-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#openAdjust"
                title="<%= t("editor.reposition_title", default: "Reframe this card's media — drag to reposition, or crop and zoom a photo") %>">
          <span><%= t("editor.reposition", default: "Reposition") %></span>
        </button>
        <%# No header-backdrop pill here — a photo or a video covers the panel
            a backdrop would paint on. The mobile background is another matter:
            it is BELOW the header, and a picture in the header says nothing
            about it. This branch used to offer it only to the three full-screen
            types and every other type with a picture had no way to design its
            phone view at all. %>
        <%= render "shared/mobile_background_cta" %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <button type="button" class="split-left-design-prompt"
              data-action="click->media-picker#open"
              title="<%= t("editor.add_design_title") %>">
        <span class="split-left-design-prompt-icon">＋</span>
        <span class="split-left-design-prompt-title"><%= t("editor.add_design") %></span>
        <span class="split-left-design-prompt-sub"><%= t("editor.add_design_sub") %></span>
      </button>
      <%# Reposition is hidden until media lands on this card without a server
          render — media_picker#_syncAdjustFab reveals it, the same
          stays-in-the-DOM contract as the design prompt above.

          Header background is offered because a card with no media is the one
          card whose panel is nothing but a colour, and on a phone setting one
          earns the card a header strip to paint it on (.split-left.has-media-bg,
          see the mobile block in application.css). media_picker#_syncAdjustFab
          hides it again if media does arrive, where it would be a control that
          does nothing. Not on the three full-screen types: the phone draws
          them no header whatever they carry, so there is nothing for a header
          backdrop to be behind — card_takes_backdrop? is that rule. %>
      <div class="split-left-cta-row">
        <%= render "shared/change_animation_cta", action: "openShapes" if is_nps %>
        <% if card_takes_backdrop?(card) %>
          <%# .bare-bg-fab is what media_picker#_syncAdjustFab toggles: this is
              the one header-backdrop pill that has to go when media lands. %>
          <button type="button" class="add-bg-fab header-bg-fab bare-bg-fab"
                  data-action="click->media-picker#openCardBackground"
                  title="<%= t("editor.header_background_title", default: "Colour or image behind this card's animation — the header on a phone") %>">
            <span><%= t("editor.header_background", default: "Header background") %></span>
          </button>
        <% end %>
        <button type="button" class="add-bg-fab media-adjust-fab"
                data-action="click->media-picker#openAdjust"
                title="<%= t("editor.reposition_title", default: "Reframe this card's media — drag to reposition, or crop and zoom a photo") %>"
                hidden>
          <span><%= t("editor.reposition", default: "Reposition") %></span>
        </button>
        <%= render "shared/mobile_background_cta" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
